# Shell scripts must reach the server with LF endings.
#
# The checkout is edited on Windows and deployed to Linux. Git's autocrlf
# converted operations/publish.sh to CRLF on the way in, and a CRLF shell script
# fails at the first line with `set: pipefail: invalid option name` -- which
# broke a deploy before this file existed.
#
# Explicit rules beat autocrlf, so these files keep LF in the repo and in every
# working tree.
*.sh text eol=lf

# CI executes the workflow on Linux.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# hexo-admin's bundle is a prebuilt artifact that ships CRLF, and
# operations/patch-editor-bundle.js preserves whatever the file uses. Leave it
# untouched so a `git checkout` gives back the exact bytes that were committed.
operations/hexo-admin-bundle.js -text
